+## Performance
+
+Measured in the steamac VM (M2, guest under FEX, wmtr transport, app-19e), d3d11bench through Proton, 12 s runs,
+variants interleaved, 4 rounds; the variant switches off one change at a time (the default build has all of
+them). fps mean (min-max):
+
+| config | all on | `d3d11.submitBeforePresent=False` | `DXMT_RESIDENCY_SET=0` | `d3d11.cpuCachedDynamicResources=True` |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| CPU-bound, 60000 draws, no fill | 79.3 (74.0-81.8) | 81.4 (79.8-82.1) | 80.3 (79.2-80.9) | 81.4 (80.9-82.2) |
+| GPU-bound, 200 draws, 12 fill passes | 40.2 (40.2-40.3) | 40.0 (39.7-40.3) | 40.0 (39.8-40.2) | 40.1 (39.9-40.2) |
+
+All differences are inside the run-to-run spread: the three changes are neutral on this load and stay (the cached
+mapping stays opt-in). hanzpo 48259b2c is measured with `d3d11bench --indexed 1` against a host library built
+without it: 51.5 fps median with it (9 runs, 35.6-51.7; the low ones in the first rounds after boot) vs 21.2-26.3 fps (4 runs) without, about 2.2x on that shader; kept. D3D12 (d3d12bench, same VM): 2000 draws + 4 fill passes 85.3 fps; ExecuteIndirect faults the GPU, as with DXMT outside the VM.
+
